      "actorCommandPolicyEvidence": {
        "completedCommandCount": 1
      },
      "actorResponse": "`moldea` is a system for maintaining durable, Git-owned project context and agent definitions. It helps coding agents consistently understand a repository over time without taking control of ordinary engineering work.\n\nInitialize it when:\n\n- You explicitly want the repository to adopt `moldea`.\n- The project’s purpose and who/what it serves are clear enough to document accurately.\n- You want durable context or agent-system knowledge versioned alongside the code.\n\nInitialization creates the adoption foundation:\n\n- `/moldea/moldea.yaml`\n- `/moldea/project.md`\n- A managed awareness block in `README.md`\n\nDon’t initialize it merely because the skill is installed, or for routine coding tasks that do not need durable project context. Initialization should be an intentional, one-time repository adoption step.",
